01:31:17.336 --> 01:31:17.970
PRESIDENT Menem and colleagues

01:31:17.970 --> 01:31:20.970
today I am introducing a

01:31:20.973 --> 01:31:23.973
resolution to support sb 417 by

01:31:25.444 --> 01:31:26.780
senator christopher her call to

01:31:26.780 --> 01:31:28.478
ban and ab 736 by

01:31:28.514 --> 01:31:29.182
assemblymember buffy wicks.

01:31:29.182 --> 01:31:31.582
Collectively these bills are

01:31:32.319 --> 01:31:35.880
known as the affordable housing

01:31:35.880 --> 01:31:35.855
bond act of 2026 and these

01:31:35.855 --> 01:31:38.255
bills were recently introduced

01:31:39.392 --> 01:31:42.195
in the state legislature to

01:31:42.195 --> 01:31:42.929
authorize a $10 billion general

01:31:42.929 --> 01:31:44.929
obligation affordable housing

01:31:45.865 --> 01:31:46.465
bond measure to be placed on

01:31:46.465 --> 01:31:48.465
the JUNE 2026 ballot.

01:31:49.870 --> 01:31:50.570
This bond would fund the

01:31:50.570 --> 01:31:52.570
construction, rehabilitation

01:31:53.273 --> 01:31:54.400
and preservation of tens of

01:31:54.400 --> 01:31:54.674
thousands of affordable housing

01:31:54.674 --> 01:31:57.740
units across the state.

01:31:57.744 --> 01:31:58.444
This resolution follows a

01:31:58.444 --> 01:32:00.844
letter recently submitted by

01:32:01.214 --> 01:32:01.881
mayor lori to state to the

01:32:01.881 --> 01:32:04.881
state in support of this

01:32:04.885 --> 01:32:05.752
legislation.

01:32:05.752 --> 01:32:09.220
If passed by the voters next

01:32:09.220 --> 01:32:09.723
year this bond would fund the

01:32:09.723 --> 01:32:11.723
construction of 35,000 new

01:32:13.260 --> 01:32:13.727
homes affordable to very low

01:32:13.727 --> 01:32:14.460
income, extremely low income

01:32:14.460 --> 01:32:16.860
and homeless families across

01:32:17.297 --> 01:32:17.597
california for at least 55

01:32:17.597 --> 01:32:18.264
years.

01:32:18.264 --> 01:32:21.100
It will also preserve and

01:32:21.100 --> 01:32:23.100
rehabilitate 42,000 existing

01:32:25.306 --> 01:32:26.600
affordable units in the face of

01:32:26.600 --> 01:32:28.406
the extreme housing crisis.

01:32:29.109 --> 01:32:29.877
Our city and state is facing.

01:32:29.877 --> 01:32:30.511
This would make a significant

01:32:30.511 --> 01:32:32.813
difference in helping san

01:32:32.813 --> 01:32:33.246
francisco meet its affordable

01:32:33.246 --> 01:32:35.246
housing need.

01:32:36.149 --> 01:32:39.320
As a city we need to build

01:32:39.320 --> 01:32:40.540
82,069 units by the year 2031

01:32:40.540 --> 01:32:43.257
to meet to meet our arena

01:32:43.257 --> 01:32:43.991
target and we are working to

01:32:43.991 --> 01:32:46.660
zone to create that capacity.

01:32:46.660 --> 01:32:47.394
But this bond is another

01:32:47.394 --> 01:32:50.264
important piece of the puzzle

01:32:50.264 --> 01:32:50.497
to provide the funding sources

01:32:50.497 --> 01:32:51.198
.

01:32:51.198 --> 01:32:53.198
additionally, 13 thousand

01:32:54.100 --> 01:32:54.735
california families will

01:32:54.735 --> 01:32:55.502
receive assistance to become

01:32:55.502 --> 01:32:58.306
home homeowners as a result of

01:32:58.306 --> 01:32:59.700
this bond and this legislation

01:32:59.700 --> 01:33:01.342
protects and prioritizes some

01:33:01.342 --> 01:33:02.109
of our state's most vulnerable

01:33:02.109 --> 01:33:05.109
populations with set asides for

01:33:05.346 --> 01:33:06.130
farmworker and tribal housing

01:33:06.130 --> 01:33:08.130
affordable housing projects

01:33:09.617 --> 01:33:10.317
in san francisco have directly

01:33:10.317 --> 01:33:12.717
benefited from the programs

01:33:13.554 --> 01:33:13.854
that would be funded by this

01:33:13.854 --> 01:33:15.854
bond.

01:33:16.223 --> 01:33:17.158
Most recently 4200 geary street

01:33:17.158 --> 01:33:19.158
a 98 unit 100% affordable

01:33:20.828 --> 01:33:21.562
apartment building for low

01:33:21.562 --> 01:33:22.230
income seniors in the richmond

01:33:22.230 --> 01:33:24.532
received a significant award

01:33:24.532 --> 01:33:25.166
from the multiple family

01:33:25.166 --> 01:33:27.166
housing program in 2021.

01:33:29.270 --> 01:33:32.240
as of today america has more

01:33:32.240 --> 01:33:32.974
than 10,000 affordable units

01:33:32.974 --> 01:33:35.974
in the development pipeline and

01:33:36.277 --> 01:33:37.120
many of these projects would

01:33:37.120 --> 01:33:37.312
most likely benefit from this

01:33:37.312 --> 01:33:39.312
bond.

01:33:40.248 --> 01:33:40.848
This bond measure is the kind

01:33:40.848 --> 01:33:42.848
of fiscally responsible

01:33:44.510 --> 01:33:44.752
investment in affordable

01:33:44.752 --> 01:33:45.153
housing that we should be

01:33:45.153 --> 01:33:47.153
encouraging.

01:33:48.189 --> 01:33:48.923
It will have no impact on the

01:33:48.923 --> 01:33:51.323
2025 2026 state budget as the

01:33:52.294 --> 01:33:55.163
bonds would not be issued until

01:33:55.163 --> 01:33:56.131
2027 at the earliest and every

01:33:56.131 --> 01:33:58.400
$1 spent by the state would be

01:33:58.400 --> 01:33:59.134
matched by $4 in federal tax

01:33:59.134 --> 01:34:01.569
credits, local grants and rent

01:34:01.569 --> 01:34:02.303
payments.

01:34:02.303 --> 01:34:04.703
Without this bond california

01:34:05.373 --> 01:34:06.730
would leave billions of dollars

01:34:06.730 --> 01:34:06.374
in federal tax credits on the

01:34:06.374 --> 01:34:08.374
table.

01:34:08.777 --> 01:34:09.611
I want to thank assembly member

01:34:09.611 --> 01:34:12.611
