01:43:21.236 --> 01:43:23.636
Today I'm introducing a

01:43:24.239 --> 01:43:24.940
resolution in support of senate

01:43:24.940 --> 01:43:26.940
bill 222 principally authored

01:43:27.510 --> 01:43:28.244
by state senator scott wiener

01:43:28.244 --> 01:43:28.978
also known as the affordable

01:43:28.978 --> 01:43:31.130
insurance and climate recovery

01:43:31.130 --> 01:43:31.681
act.

01:43:31.681 --> 01:43:32.448
The bill will hold oil

01:43:32.448 --> 01:43:34.848
companies responsible for their

01:43:35.184 --> 01:43:35.751
role in our worsening climate

01:43:35.751 --> 01:43:36.452
and insurance crises.

01:43:36.452 --> 01:43:39.188
Every year our planet goes

01:43:39.188 --> 01:43:39.922
through more frequent and more

01:43:39.922 --> 01:43:41.922
devastating climate disasters.

01:43:42.190 --> 01:43:45.462
In 2024 we endured a series of

01:43:45.462 --> 01:43:46.162
atmospheric rivers that flooded

01:43:46.162 --> 01:43:46.863
san francisco and damaged or

01:43:46.863 --> 01:43:49.165
destroyed numerous homes and

01:43:49.165 --> 01:43:50.320
trees.

01:43:50.320 --> 01:43:51.968
The damages from those storms

01:43:51.968 --> 01:43:52.502
totaled $4.5 billion just just

01:43:52.502 --> 01:43:52.969
a few months ago.

01:43:52.969 --> 01:43:54.969
San francisco.

01:43:55.905 --> 01:43:56.672
San francisco deployed our own

01:43:56.672 --> 01:43:59.408
firefighters to help battle the

01:43:59.408 --> 01:44:01.808
los angeles wildfires which

01:44:02.579 --> 01:44:04.979
burned 58.4. Five square miles

01:44:05.515 --> 01:44:06.216
of land, destroyed 16,200

01:44:06.216 --> 01:44:08.616
structures displayed tens of

01:44:09.118 --> 01:44:09.853
thousands of families and

01:44:09.853 --> 01:44:12.253
caused $250 billion in damage.

01:44:12.989 --> 01:44:13.756
these climate disasters have

01:44:13.756 --> 01:44:16.156
prompted insurance providers to

01:44:16.626 --> 01:44:17.493
exponentially raise their rates

01:44:17.493 --> 01:44:19.329
with some rates going up by as

01:44:19.329 --> 01:44:21.329
much as 48% in 2024.

01:44:23.990 --> 01:44:23.867
Beyond that, providers have

01:44:23.867 --> 01:44:26.403
declined to renew more than 2.8

01:44:26.403 --> 01:44:27.137
million homeowner policies

01:44:27.137 --> 01:44:29.537
in california between 2020 and

01:44:30.807 --> 01:44:31.574
2022, including 531,000 homes

01:44:31.574 --> 01:44:34.710
in los angeles county, many of

01:44:34.710 --> 01:44:35.178
which were destroyed by the

01:44:35.178 --> 01:44:35.711
palisades fire.

01:44:35.711 --> 01:44:38.111
With nowhere to go,

01:44:38.715 --> 01:44:39.483
policyholders must resort to

01:44:39.483 --> 01:44:40.250
using the state's fair plan the

01:44:40.250 --> 01:44:43.120
final option available for fire

01:44:43.120 --> 01:44:43.787
insurance or even the fair

01:44:43.787 --> 01:44:44.587
plan, however, has had to

01:44:44.587 --> 01:44:46.756
significantly raise the cost of

01:44:46.756 --> 01:44:47.491
coverage for policy holders as

01:44:47.491 --> 01:44:47.958
the costs of climate disasters

01:44:47.958 --> 01:44:49.958
have increased.

01:44:50.894 --> 01:44:51.594
It is simply unfair and

01:44:51.594 --> 01:44:53.594
inexcusable for policyholders

01:44:54.298 --> 01:44:55.132
to be forced to pay the price

01:44:55.132 --> 01:44:55.866
for a climate crisis that has

01:44:55.866 --> 01:44:58.702
mostly been caused by oil

01:44:58.702 --> 01:44:59.536
companies.

01:44:59.536 --> 01:45:00.404
sb 222 will create a private

01:45:00.404 --> 01:45:02.940
right of action so that those

01:45:02.940 --> 01:45:03.674
injured by climate disasters

01:45:03.674 --> 01:45:06.176
will be able to recover their

01:45:06.176 --> 01:45:06.843
losses from the oil and gas

01:45:06.843 --> 01:45:07.544
companies that misled the

01:45:07.544 --> 01:45:10.413
public for decades about their

01:45:10.413 --> 01:45:10.747
contribution to the climate

01:45:10.747 --> 01:45:11.516
crisis.

01:45:11.516 --> 01:45:14.510
the bill will also create a

01:45:14.510 --> 01:45:14.719
direct cause of action for

01:45:14.719 --> 01:45:15.352
insurers against these same

01:45:15.352 --> 01:45:17.388
companies and allow the

01:45:17.388 --> 01:45:18.155
insurers to recover for harms

01:45:18.155 --> 01:45:18.889
to their businesses that result

01:45:18.889 --> 01:45:21.889
from climate related impacts an

01:45:21.925 --> 01:45:22.593
increase in costs through the

01:45:22.593 --> 01:45:22.926
volatility of the insurance

01:45:22.926 --> 01:45:24.926
market.

01:45:24.928 --> 01:45:25.662
finally and certain

01:45:25.662 --> 01:45:26.330
circumstances this bill will

01:45:26.330 --> 01:45:29.330
require the fair plan to

01:45:29.433 --> 01:45:30.168
exercise its right of

01:45:30.168 --> 01:45:32.637
subrogation against oil and gas

01:45:32.637 --> 01:45:33.270
companies to recover claims

01:45:33.270 --> 01:45:35.670
paid toward large climate

01:45:36.574 --> 01:45:36.807
driven events such as wildfires

01:45:36.807 --> 01:45:37.608
.

01:45:37.608 --> 01:45:38.342
I want to thank senator wiener

01:45:38.342 --> 01:45:40.277
for authoring this legislation

01:45:40.277 --> 01:45:40.911
and I also want to thank conor

01:45:40.911 --> 01:45:41.645
johnston with the extreme

01:45:41.645 --> 01:45:43.814
